{"book":"Job","chapter":26,"translation":"KJV","url":"/bible/job/26","verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"But Job answered and said,","words":[["But Job",["H347"]],["answered",["H6030"]],["and said,",[]]]},{"verse":2,"text":"How hast thou helped him that is without power? how savest thou the arm that hath no strength?","words":[["How hast thou helped",["H5826"]],["him that is without power?",["H3581"]],["how savest",["H3467"]],["thou the arm",["H2220"]],["that hath no",["H3808"]],["strength?",[]]]},{"verse":3,"text":"How hast thou counselled him that hath no wisdom? and how hast thou plentifully declared the thing as it is?","words":[["How hast thou counselled",["H3289"]],["him that hath no",["H3808"]],["wisdom?",["H2451"]],["and how hast thou plentifully",["H7230"]],["declared",["H3045"]],["the thing as it is?",[]]]},{"verse":4,"text":"To whom hast thou uttered words? and whose spirit came from thee?","words":[["To whom hast thou uttered",["H5046"]],["words?",["H4405"]],["and whose spirit",["H5397"]],["came from thee?",[]]]},{"verse":5,"text":"Dead things are formed from under the waters, and the inhabitants thereof.","words":[["Dead",["H7496"]],["things are formed",["H2342"]],["from under the waters,",["H4325"]],["and the inhabitants thereof.",[]]]},{"verse":6,"text":"Hell is naked before him, and destruction hath no covering.","words":[["Hell",["H7585"]],["is naked",["H6174"]],["before him, and destruction",["H11"]],["hath no covering.",[]]]},{"verse":7,"text":"He stretcheth out the north over the empty place, and hangeth the earth upon nothing.","words":[["He stretcheth out",["H5186"]],["the north",["H6828"]],["over the empty place,",["H8414"]],["and hangeth",["H8518"]],["the earth",["H776"]],["upon nothing.",[]]]},{"verse":8,"text":"He bindeth up the waters in his thick clouds; and the cloud is not rent under them.","words":[["He bindeth up",["H6887"]],["the waters",["H4325"]],["in his thick clouds;",["H5645"]],["and the cloud",["H6051"]],["is not rent under them.",[]]]},{"verse":9,"text":"He holdeth back the face of his throne, and spreadeth his cloud upon it.","words":[["He holdeth back",["H270"]],["the face",["H6440"]],["of his throne,",["H3678"]],["and spreadeth",["H6576"]],["his cloud upon it.",[]]]},{"verse":10,"text":"He hath compassed the waters with bounds, until the day and night come to an end.","words":[["He hath compassed",["H2328"]],["the waters",["H6440","H4325"]],["with bounds,",["H2706"]],["until the day",["H216"]],["and night",["H2822"]],["come to an end.",[]]]},{"verse":11,"text":"The pillars of heaven tremble and are astonished at his reproof.","words":[["The pillars",["H5982"]],["of heaven",["H8064"]],["tremble",["H7322"]],["and are astonished",["H8539"]],["at his reproof.",[]]]},{"verse":12,"text":"He divideth the sea with his power, and by his understanding he smiteth through the proud.","words":[["He divideth",["H7280"]],["the sea",["H3220"]],["with his power,",["H3581"]],["and by his understanding",["H8394","H8394"]],["he smiteth",["H4272"]],["through the proud.",[]]]},{"verse":13,"text":"By his spirit he hath garnished the heavens; his hand hath formed the crooked serpent.","words":[["By his spirit",["H7307"]],["he hath garnished",["H8235"]],["the heavens;",["H8064"]],["his hand",["H3027"]],["hath formed",["H2342"]],["the crooked",["H1281"]],["serpent.",[]]]},{"verse":14,"text":"Lo, these are parts of his ways: but how little a portion is heard of him? but the thunder of his power who can understand?","words":[["Lo, these are parts",["H7098"]],["of his ways:",["H1870"]],["but how little",["H8102"]],["a portion",["H1697"]],["is heard",["H8085"]],["of him? but the thunder",["H7482"]],["of his power",["H1369"]],["who can understand?",[]]]}]}